[E0436] Error: `text` is used after `owner`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/333_var_pattern_moves/main.wip:17:10 ]
    │
 15 │     var (n, text) = (1, owner.toStr())
    │             ──┬─  
    │               ╰─── `text` borrows `owner`
 16 │     owner.push("d")
    │     ──┬──  
    │       ╰──── `owner` passed as `&var` here
 17 │     n += text.len()
    │          ──┬─  
    │            ╰─── used here
    │ 
    │ Help: use `text` before `owner` changes, or keep a copy that owns its bytes with `String::of(…)`
    │ 
    │ Note: a `str` points into the bytes of what it borrows, so those must not change while the `str` is still used
────╯
